# GitHub Pages

The live site is **Deploy from a branch → `gh-pages` → `/(root)`**.

`web/` on `main` is the source. `gh-pages` is a **flattened copy of `web/`** (index at repo root, not `web/index.html`).

Pushing `main` does **not** update https://florentinhortopan.github.io/Kanarin/

## After any commit that touches `web/`

```bash
./scripts/publish-pages.sh
```

That copies `HEAD:web` onto `gh-pages` and pushes. Do it in the same turn as the `main` push. Do not wait for the user to notice the old page.

## Do not

- Point Pages at GitHub Actions / `actions/deploy-pages` — that fights the branch setup
- Commit `.github/workflows/` unless the user has `workflow` scope (it was rejected once)
- Leave the live site on an old `gh-pages` SHA after shipping `web/` changes
